{
	"generator": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-caterina-projects/028cfc19-e94f-5159-b63f-0777236533aa/scratchpad/fixtures/gen_fixtures.py (not committed; run with uv inside the interferometry repo)",
	"conventions": {
		"units": "Hold t = 1; rates in 1/t; QFI in t^2; true omega = 0.",
		"basis": "Qubit |0>,|1>; s_a = sigma_a/2, s_z = diag(+1/2,-1/2); sigma_- = |0><1|, sigma_+ = |1><0|.",
		"siteOrder": "Qubits S (0..nS-1) then A (nS..N-1); site 0 is the most significant bit of the 2^N index. With pseudomodes, the modes are appended after all qubits (mode k belongs to qubit k) and start in vacuum; psiFull is the qubit part only (length 2^N).",
		"pseudomodeLayout": "The Python engine gives every qubit its own mode whenever the register has pseudomodes, even qubits that are not coupled (e.g. a clean ancilla): uncoupled modes stay in vacuum and are only traced out. A TS port may drop them; the qubit marginal and QFI are unchanged.",
		"vectorisation": "Row-major vec(rho)[i*D+j] = rho[i,j]; vec(A rho B) = (A kron B^T) vec(rho).",
		"generator": "dH/domega = J_z^S + ancillaWeight * J_z^A (setup.ancillaWeight; 0 passive, 1 active).",
		"controls": "TS layout, length 15 + 6K: [0,9) alpha_ij (index 3i+j, i over S axes x,y,z, j over A axes), [9,12) b (field on J^A), [12,15) c (field on J^S), [15,15+3K) pulse rotation vectors v_A on A, [15+3K,15+6K) v_S on S (zeros when the Python setup had s_pulses=False). H_ctrl = sum alpha_ij J_i^S J_j^A + b.J^A + c.J^S (+ bias * generator for MZI cases). Pulse q is exp(-i(v_A.J^A + v_S.J^S)). 'pythonParams' is the engine's own vector (length 21 without S pulses, 27 with).",
		"strang": "M steps of dt = t/M: U(dt/2) N(dt) U(dt/2) each, with U(tau) = exp(-i H tau), H = H_ctrl + H_bath. Adjacent half steps fuse. Pulses sit at step boundaries pulseBoundaries (1..M-1): after step b's trailing U(dt/2), before step b+1's leading U(dt/2). Python places pulse q at seg*(q+1), seg = M/(K+1), K = 2; pulseTimes = boundary/M. At 2M steps the boundaries double. Pulses with an all-zero vector are skipped by Python (no effect).",
		"derivative": "drho/domega is propagated exactly: for each U(tau) use the block exponential exp([[A, B],[0, A]]) with A = -i tau [H,.], B = -i tau [G,.] (or the Hilbert-space equivalent); noise and pulses do not depend on omega.",
		"markovNoise": "Per qubit, Lindblad step expm(L dt) with: dephasing gamma -> sqrt(gamma/2) sigma_z (coherence e^{-gamma t}); amplitudeDamping gamma -> sqrt(gamma(nbar+1)) sigma_-, plus sqrt(gamma nbar) sigma_+ when nbar > 0; depolarizing gamma -> sqrt(gamma/4) sigma_a, a=x,y,z; transverse gamma -> sqrt(gamma/2) sigma_x. All terms of one particle share one generator (exact step). Python cases (source 'engine') use the equal Kraus forms; the script asserts Lindblad == Kraus for the single-channel limits.",
		"lorentzianNoise": "One damped mode per noisy qubit, truncated at pmLevels Fock levels, damping L = sqrt(2 lambda) b. dephasing: H_bath += sqrt(gamma lambda) s_z (b + b^dag). amplitudeDamping (Python channel 'non_markovian_ad', coupling 'jc'): H_bath += sqrt(gamma lambda / 2)(sigma_+ b + sigma_- b^dag). lorentzianMethod 'pseudomodes' = this explicit model; 'closedForm' = uncontrolled steps=1 hold whose noise is the mask rho_ab -> rho_ab exp(-Gamma(t) d_H(a,b)) with Gamma(t) = gamma [t - (1 - e^{-lambda t})/lambda] (Python dephasing_mask_superop), applied as the single N of the one Strang step.",
		"cleanAncilla": "Case c05 (Python clean_ancilla=True): noise acts only on S; ancilla noise is all zeros.",
		"input": "setup.input 'sym': psi is in Sym(S) (x) Sym(A), basis index mS*(nA+1) + mA, where column m of Sym(n) is the normalised Dicke state with m qubits in |1> (J_z = n/2 - m) (Python product_isometry ordering, S first). psiFull = iso @ psi in the qubit space. 'full' (MZI): psi == psiFull.",
		"qfi": "SLD QFI 2 sum_{l_i+l_j > 1e-10} |<i|drho|j>|^2/(l_i+l_j) of the qubit marginal. 'qfi' at 'steps', 'qfi2M' at 2*steps (when steps > 1), 'qfiAtSteps' for extra step counts, 'trace' = Tr rho of the qubit marginal.",
		"mzi": "MZI cases: nA = 0, generator J_z^T, controls zero, 'bias' adds bias * J_z^T to H (Python mzi_hold detuning). Covariant channels use one exact step (steps=1).",
		"readouts": "readout_fishers optimises the rotations internally, so readout cases record values at fixed rotations instead. ep(obs) = slope^2/var with mean = Tr(rho obs), slope = Tr(drho obs), var = Tr(rho obs^2) - mean^2 (parity: var = 1 - mean^2); 0 if var <= 1e-9 (Python _ep). R(u) = exp(-i sum_k u_k J_k) on the given register. ep_s: obs = R_S(uS)^dag J_z^S R_S(uS); parity_s: obs = R_S^dag P_S R_S with P_S = prod_{k in S} sigma_z^(k). ep_joint (x of length 7): obs = cos(x6) R_S(x0:3)^dag J_z^S R_S + sin(x6) R_A(x3:6)^dag J_z^A R_A. parity_joint: R = R_S(x0:3) R_A(x3:6), obs = R^dag P_{S+A} R. rho, drho are those of case 'fromCase'.",
		"random": "Controls ~ N(0,1) clipped to +-10 (alpha,b,c) and +-2pi (pulses), psi = normalised complex Gaussian; both drawn from numpy default_rng(seed) in that order (seed recorded per case)."
	},
